[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408594606","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111694#issuecomment-3408594606","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111694","id":3408594606,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LKwau","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T23:08:41Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T23:08:41Z","body":"Making dedicated `.syntax.cpp` files seems a bit superfluous. Couldn't the headers *themselves* be set as the target, or maybe just exclude a target entirely? We shouldn't have to worry about any cleanup after the fact ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408594606/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408603055","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111694#issuecomment-3408603055","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111694","id":3408603055,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LKyev","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T23:12:50Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T23:12:50Z","body":"As far as I know - and from what I tried - we can't run compilation on header files, so we need to create dummy files. And the only native way to check for header completeness is through compilation with the `-fsyntax-only` or equivalent flag. \r\n\r\nI could be entirely wrong, but I couldn't make it work directly on headers, hence the roundabout method. I would also prefer a cleaner method, especially since the cleanup is not ideal, as it can be skipped if the process is killed completely. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408603055/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3409923911","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111694#issuecomment-3409923911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111694","id":3409923911,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LP09H","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T09:09:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T09:09:58Z","body":"Running a build command on a `.h` file works file for me, with `clang` on macOS. Practically, I don't think compilers care about the difference. \r\nThe only possible problem I can think of is that your compiler might treat `.h` as a C header instead of a C++ header?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3409923911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412668715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111694#issuecomment-3412668715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111694","id":3412668715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LaTEr","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T20:09:59Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T20:09:59Z","body":"This might be an SCons thing… I recall the `Object` emitter relying on a suffix to change behavior. It might need something manually assigned; will do some tests now","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412668715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418464583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111694#issuecomment-3418464583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111694","id":3418464583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LwaFH","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_i