url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-18T16:47:42Z","updated_at":"2025-10-18T16:48:09Z","body":"Ok so [this](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/master...StarryWorm:godot:syntax-only-direct-h) is the best I could come up with. It uses Scons Actions directly for the header files.\r\nThanks to that it doesn't need the whole `.syntax.cpp` workaround. But it does go through a unique pathway that isn't the one used for source files. \r\n\r\nOne funny issue which I can't seem to solve: it prints both the compiling message and the filename for the header files. Seems like it comes from scons' internal itself, couldnt do anything to suppress it (tried various workarounds, none worked). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418648731/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]